quests":8}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"fec117fa58e21295735419d8804308efa33979040ad8ca849dfd7d7c90fff1b6"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:G1G2","usage":{"input_tokens":199805,"output_tokens":7094,"requests":13}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"6aaf2e363b9ad0dc04efa039c539136e13e920b34f02b7c7595b239811e92823"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:project.symbol-reference-completeness","usage":{"input_tokens":214712,"output_tokens":4099,"requests":8}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a proving command (or extend AC15's harness) that exercises at least the Tier-1 mutating paths (AC1-AC7) against a REBAR_TRACKER_DIR outside the repo root, so DD1's claim 'each routed through the resolver' is verified at runtime, not only by the static boundary checker.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e"],"criteria":["E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["DD1: 'AC1-AC13 hold, each routed through config.tracker_dir()... Verify: python scripts/check_tickets_boundary.py'","AC14 script 'rejects new store-path composition in src/' — a grep-style static gate, not a runtime exercise","Only AC15/AC17 exercise a relocated store, and only for bridge_status (AC9)"],"finding":"DD1 proves AC1-AC13 via `python scripts/check_tickets_boundary.py`, but that script is a STATIC boundary-checker (AC14) that can only prove the absence of new hardcoded path composition — it cannot prove that the mutating paths AC1-AC7 actually read/write the RELOCATED store at runtime. Only AC9 (bridge_status) gets a runtime relocation test (AC15/AC17); the other mutating siblings (binding_store, reconcile snapshot, check_store_compat, BRIDGE_ALERT write, commit-back, delivery subprocess, projects_store) have no proving command that exercises them against a relocated store.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4d62c5445bb76eb4","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Definition of Done DD1; ACs 1-7","norm_id":"n70fe5a3d20cf5271","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A fix for AC1 (binding_store) that routes through config.tracker_dir() but resolves the wrong sub-path would pass the static boundary checker and pass DD4's default-layout suites, yet still write to the wrong relocated location"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add a DD entry: an integration test setting REBAR_TRACKER_DIR outside repo_root that drives each Tier-1 mutating path and asserts the artifact (binding store, prev_snapshot.json, BRIDGE_ALERT event, sync mapping) materializes under the relocated dir and NOT under repo_root/.tickets-tracker.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify in AC2/AC5 how prev_snapshot.json (and commit-back staging) persists between reconcile passes when the store is an ABSOLUTE path OUTSIDE the repo worktree, since the GHA commit-back step stages only the repo worktree and cannot reach an out-of-tree store.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0222,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["reconcile.py:315-317 (in-code): 'Writing to the tracker dir ensures the snapshot survives between runs because the workflow's commit-back step commits everything under that directory.'","reconcile.py:318: `tracker_dir = repo_root / \".tickets-tracker\"  # tickets-boundary-ok`","Observed failure names an absolute out-of-tree store (/var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets) — that path is not inside the repo git worktree the commit-back step stages"],"finding":"AC2 and AC5 do not address that a store relocated to an ABSOLUTE path OUTSIDE the repo worktree (the exact deployed case: REBAR_TRACKER_DIR=/var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets) cannot be persisted by the GHA commit-back step, which stages the repo worktree. reconcile.py:310-318 explicitly documents that prev_snapshot.json is written under .tickets-tracker BECAUSE 'the workflow's commit-back step commits everything under that directory' to survive ephemeral GHA runs. Merely resolving the write root to the relocated store (AC2) means prev_snapshot.json lands out-of-tree and is never committed, silently reverting the reconciler to re-deriving all 2050+ inbound_create mutations every pass.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6e0b59a131bd18ae","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria AC2 / AC5; src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile.py:310-321","norm_id":"n5323b54d4afc460a","priority":0.7778,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Deployed MCP server with REBAR_TRACKER_DIR set to an absolute out-of-tree path runs a persist reconcile pass; prev_snapshot.json is written to the relocated store but the commit-back step (repo-rooted git add) never stages it, so the next GHA run sees prev_snapshot={} and re-derives every mutation"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Enumerate `_cli/_bridge_commands.py:189` as a second caller of `last_pass.snapshot` for AC8/AC9, or state the fix resolves the store internally in last_pass (via config.tracker_dir()) so both callers are covered without a call-site change.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["src/rebar/_lib_ops.py:289-292 `last_pass = _engine_module(...); result = last_pass.snapshot(root, ...)` — the enumerated caller","src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py:187-193 `last_pass = importlib.import_module('rebar_reconciler.last_pass'); result = last_pass.snapshot(Path(config.repo_root()), ...)` — an UNenumerated second caller passing repo_root","src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/last_pass.py:74 `resolve_environment_id(repo_root, ...)` and :89 `path = repo_root / '.tickets-tracker' / '.env-id'` — both callers reach the defective compose"],"finding":"AC8/AC9 name `_lib_ops.py:288` as the caller feeding repo_root into `last_pass.snapshot`/`resolve_environment_id`, but a second in-process caller — `_cli/_bridge_commands.py:189-190` (the CLI `bridge status` path) — also passes `Path(config.repo_root())` into `last_pass.snapshot`. It is not enumerated. If the fix threads a resolved tracker into last_pass (as DD1's 'routed through config.tracker_dir() or ReconcilerSettings.tracker_dir' phrasing suggests) rather than resolving the store internally, this CLI caller must also be updated or `rebar bridge status` on the CLI still composes the wrong path.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe4e0082c4949533d","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC8/AC9 + Root cause section ('the caller _lib_ops.py:288 passes the repo root')","norm_id":"nda0cdce63d778a70","priority":0.75,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Operator runs `rebar bridge status` on the CLI (not via MCP) against a relocated store — still hits the `.env-id` ENOENT if the fix only touched the MCP/_lib_ops caller."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Resolve the tracker inside `last_pass.snapshot`/`resolve_environment_id` via `config.tracker_dir()` so both `_lib_ops.py:288` and `_cli/_bridge_commands.py:189` are fixed by one change; otherwise add the CLI caller to AC8/AC9's edit set.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"no